WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:13.286
was lost.

2
00:00:14.126 --> 00:00:16.388
It seemed that no one had heard him cry for help.

3
00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:20.312
But just when he was about to lose hope, he heard footsteps.

4
00:00:20.332 --> 00:00:27.097
"Good afternoon, Pinocchio," said a fox as it walked up to him.

5
00:00:28.498 --> 00:00:30.020
The fox was leaning on a cane.

6
00:00:30.808 --> 00:00:34.090
To his side was a blind cat with bandages over his eyes.

7
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.132
"Who are you?"

8
00:00:36.692 --> 00:00:37.493
asked Pinocchio.

9
00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:40.195
"How do you know my name?"

10
00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:46.259
"We have seen your father, Geppetto, calling for you in the village.

11
00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:52.623
He has asked all of the villagers for help, but no one knows where to find you," said

12
00:00:52.663 --> 00:00:53.083
the cat.

13
00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:57.446
"Poor father, searching for me in the cold.

14
00:00:58.167 --> 00:00:59.388
He must be worried.

15
00:01:00.112 --> 00:01:03.914
I must hurry home to show him we are rich," Pinocchio said.

16
00:01:05.715 --> 00:01:10.258
When they heard this, the cat peeked out from under the bandage and the fox stood straighter.

17
00:01:10.838 --> 00:01:12.239
But, Pinocchio did not notice.

18
00:01:13.099 --> 00:01:14.740
"What? Rich?"

19
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.381
asked the fox.

20
00:01:16.401 --> 00:01:20.763
"How could a small wooden boy be rich?"

21
00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:26.526
"I uh I earned the money," Pinocchio lied.

22
00:01:26.546 --> 00:01:28.147
"Earned it?

23
00:01:28.647 --> 00:01:30.560
How?" asked the cat.

24
00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:37.443
"I worked as a dancer for the marionette master, and he paid me," Pinocchio lied again.

25
00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:44.366
"I don't believe such a small boy like you could have a lot of money.

26
00:01:44.386 --> 00:01:49.188
I would have to see it to believe such a thing," said the cat.

27
00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:53.910
"Well, you can't see it," said Pinocchio.

28
00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.931
"I have hidden it away."

29
00:01:56.591 --> 00:02:00.785
He didn't think about how strange it was for a blind cat to ask to see his gold.

30
00:02:00.805 --> 00:02:08.051
"It's a shame you can't take home more than a pocketful of money to Geppetto," said the fox.

31
00:02:08.071 --> 00:02:10.913
"He is such a kind man.

32
00:02:11.694 --> 00:02:16.758
I know of a way to make a small bit of money into a large load of money,

33
00:02:17.418 --> 00:02:20.141
but I'm sure you wouldn't be interested.

34
00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:21.602
Come, Mr.

35
00:02:21.682 --> 00:02:24.524
Cat, let's show Pinocchio the way home."

36
00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:29.068
"You mean I could have more money?"

37
00:02:29.612 --> 00:02:32.173
Pinocchio asked, surprised at this new idea.

38
00:02:32.193 --> 00:02:35.274
"Would I have to work for it?"

39
00:02:35.514 --> 00:02:36.134
"Oh no!"

40
00:02:37.594 --> 00:02:38.555
the cat said, laughing.

41
00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:42.216
"We would never suggest such a silly thing.

42
00:02:43.356 --> 00:02:46.817
We know of a secret field called the Field of Follies.

43
00:02:47.457 --> 00:02:53.439
If you plant your money in that field at midnight, water it, and come back the next day,

44
00:02:54.059 --> 00:02:55.940
it will have grown into a money tree."

45
00:02:58.784 --> 00:03:01.465
"Wow, then we would be really rich!"

46
00:03:01.886 --> 00:03:02.666
Pinocchio said.

47
00:03:03.346 --> 00:03:04.287
He could imagine Mr.

48
00:03:04.347 --> 00:03:07.508
Cricket telling him that honest work was the best way to be rich.

49
00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:12.470
"But, Geppetto would love me so much more if I was rich now.

50
00:03:13.591 --> 00:03:16.752
Please, would you show me this Field of Follies?"

51
00:03:19.214 --> 00:03:21.455
So, off they went to find the Field of Follies.

52
00:03:22.215 --> 00:03:24.296
They walked all day and into the evening.

53
00:03:27.976 --> 00:03:32.159
"Welcome to the Field of Follies, Pinocchio," said the cat.

54
00:03:32.179 --> 00:03:36.301
"Plant your gold wherever you want your money tree to grow!"

55
00:03:38.182 --> 00:03:39.643
Pinocchio was very excited.

56
00:03:40.103 --> 00:03:44.486
He dug a hole, carefully placed his gold inside, and covered the hole with dirt.

57
00:03:44.506 --> 00:03:47.768
"Now, you must water it.

58
00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:54.212
Mr. Cat and I will guard the money while you run to get some water," said the fox.

59
00:03:55.404 --> 00:03:58.786
Pinocchio did not think it was strange for a blind cat to stand guard.

60
00:03:59.847 --> 00:04:02.729
He ran off and quickly returned with a bucket of water.

61
00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:07.012
After the gold had been watered, there was nothing left to do but wait.

62
00:04:09.113 --> 00:04:14.117
"Now, let's go find a nearby barn so we can rest," said the cat.

63
00:04:14.137 --> 00:04:21.441
"Yes, if we stay here and watch, the tree will not grow," agreed the fox.

64
00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.804
So, off they went with happy thoughts of being rich.
